   "evidence": "A grep of ./mathlib for `nnrealCast_` finds no declarations. The \u211d\u22650 \u2192 \u211d map is `NNReal.toReal`: `Mathlib/Basic/NNReal/Defs.lean:254` has `coe_toRealHom : \u21d1toRealHom = toReal`, and `Mathlib/Basic/NNReal/Basic.lean:80` has `NNReal.coe_sum`. By contrast, `Mathlib/Data/Rat/Init.lean:60` defines `Rat.instNNRatCast : NNRatCast \u211a`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Combinatorics/Network/Nonnegative.lean",
   "fix": "Rename it after the actual coercion, e.g. `toReal_arrowSum` (the vendored rule says coercions are named after the underlying function) or `NNReal.coe_arrowSum` (matching `NNReal.coe_sum`), and update the example that uses it.",
   "issue": "`nnrealCast_arrowSum` names the \u211d\u22650 \u2192 \u211d coercion `nnrealCast`. That is not Mathlib terminology: the coercion is `NNReal.toReal`, and its lemmas are named `coe_*`. Its sibling `nnratCast_arrowSum` is fine, because \u211a\u22650 \u2192 \u211a really is `NNRat.cast`.",
   "line": 0
  }
